# Documentation

Write for a reviewer who has never opened the repo.

- Active voice, short sentences, current truth only. Remove stale “later” plans after shipping.
- `README.md`: setup, scripts, env, two-client run.
- `Overview.md`: scope and acceptance criteria.
- `RULES.md`: standards. `AGENTS.md`: contributor workflow.
- `Memory.md`: decisions, open questions, progress. No secrets or private user content.
- `docs/`: architecture, API, data, room names, snapshot format, test evidence.
- Update docs in the same change as setup or contract changes.
- State what Redis/multi-instance tests actually proved. No unmeasured scale claims.
- Define workspace, page, role, room, snapshot, and awareness on first use.
